   ],
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Arndt states classes A-D; only C is placed (copied from a B manuscript and corrected/supplemented from a lost complete A exemplar), so C is put under B with contamination from A. No relation of D (corrupt, all lack the first preface) to A/B is stated; D is treated as its own class-branch. B has only books I-VI (B1 later supplemented), so witness sets differ by book."
